"{\"url\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/project/prj_1JTZ7NRK81S0GA0S\",\"title\":\"B10 - Brondal #1 — Isometric\",\"head\":[\"UNDER VALIDATION\",\"BICRS\",\"B10 - Brondal #1\",\"B10\",\"->\",\"PROJECT DETAILS\",\"Expected first certificates\",\"2026\",\"Project code\",\"8WQK\",\"PROTOCOL DETAILS\",\"Current protocol version\"],\"issued_header\":null,\"buffer_header\":null,\"crediting\":null,\"verifier\":null,\"code\":\"8WQK\",\"approval\":\"\",\"protocol_current\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\",\"protocol_baseline\":null,\"cert_issued\":null,\"cert_retired\":null,\"cert_buffer\":null,\"reversal\":null,\"showing\":[\"Showing 2 of 2\"],\"tables\":[{\"heads\":[\"Submission date\",\"Title\",\"Download\"],\"rows\":[[\"05 Jan 2026\",\"Public Comment Summary\",\"PDF | ->\"],[\"26 Nov 2025\",\"PDD\",\"PDF | ->\"]]}],\"links\":[{\"h\":\"https://b10-char.com\",\"t\":\"B10\"},{\"h\":\"/protocol/biochar/1.1\",\"t\":\"Biochar Production and Storage v1.1\"},{\"h\":\"/supplier/spl_1JT309WR61S0FTZR\",\"t\":\"Learn more\"},{\"h\":\"https://registry.isometric.com/standard#validation-and-verification-process\",\"t\":\"Isometric Standard\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JT309WR61S0FTZR/prj_1JTZ7NRK81S0GA0S/pjd_1KE6QNCKJ1S0P1H4/public_comment_summary.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1JT309WR61S0FTZR/prj_1JTZ7NRK81S0GA0S/pjd_1KB0BX68X1S0VJ2B/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"UNDER VALIDATION\\nBICRS\\nB10 - Brondal #1\\nB10\\n->\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nExpected first certificates\\n2026\\nProject code\\n8WQK\\nPROTOCOL DETAILS\\nCurrent protocol version\\nBiochar Production and Storage v1.1\\nSummary\\n\\nB10 partners with local sawmills in White River, SA to produce biochar from wood chips created from the plantation grown timber waste streams. Using a purpose-built pyrolysis facility, the process ensures emissions control, efficiency, quality, and operational safety. The biochar is used in anaerobic digesters or inoculated and both streams end up as fertilizer/soil enhancer in agriculture.\\n\\nSouth Africa\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nBiomass Carbon Removal and Storage (BiCRS) involves storing the carbon contained in waste biomass—organic material from living or recently living organisms. BiCRS works by halting or slowing the decomposition of biomass, enabling the carbon it contains to be stored long-term. This can be achieved by converting biomass into materials that decompose more slowly—such as biochar or bio-oil—or by storing it in environments where decomposition is slowed. For BiCRS to count as carbon removal, the biomass must be replenished to ensure additional carbon dioxide is drawn from the atmosphere.\\n\\nLearn more\\nProject timeline\\nCompleted 25 Dec 2025\\nPublic comment period\\nCompleted 2025\\nInitial documentation submission\\nCompleted 2025\\nAudit kick-off\\nCompleted 2025\\nSite visit\\nExpected 2026\\nIN PROGRESS\\nApproval date\\n\\nIsometric officially approves the project having reviewed the validation report produced by the VVB, documenting the activities, results, and conclusion of the audit. A full list of content requirements for the report can be found in the Isometric Standard.\\n\\nExpected 2026\\nInitial credit issuance\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n05 Jan 2026\\tPublic Comment Summary\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n26 Nov 2025\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 2 of 2\\nPrevious\\nNext\"}"